1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,637
This is explainer-video: a skill that lets an
agent make narrated, animated explainers.

2
00:00:05,677 --> 00:00:07,545
This video was made with it.

3
00:00:08,433 --> 00:00:10,193
You describe the topic.

4
00:00:10,233 --> 00:00:15,487
The agent writes the script with you, animates it
on free draft audio, and only then pays for the

5
00:00:15,527 --> 00:00:17,093
real voice.

6
00:00:17,133 --> 00:00:21,520
Then it renders every scene with Manim, and checks
the result.

7
00:00:22,533 --> 00:00:28,226
The voice returns a timestamp for every character.
So when I say now, the picture moves.

8
00:00:28,266 --> 00:00:33,303
The same timestamps cut the captions, so they land
on the words too.

9
00:00:34,297 --> 00:00:38,869
Every new cut is its own folder, so earlier
versions stay intact.

10
00:00:39,382 --> 00:00:45,000
Sentences are cached by their text, so a shorter
edit only pays for what changed.

11
00:00:45,997 --> 00:00:51,762
Before delivery, the kit checks decoding, loudness
and caption timing, and Whisper listens to every

12
00:00:51,802 --> 00:00:53,356
sentence.

13
00:00:54,464 --> 00:00:58,758
Clone the repo, link the skill, and ask your agent
for a video.

